<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAfrican assembly approves new tax service bill.</title>
<headline>SAfrican assembly approves new tax service bill.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's national assembly on Tuesday approved a revenue service bill which Finance Minister Trevor Manuel said was aimed at streamlining the government's ability to collect taxes.</p>
<p>He told the assembly the bill would create the South African Revenue Service, which would have more autonomy than current tax collecting organs and &quot;the ability to engage in any activity to promote proper, efficient and effective tax administration.&quot;</p>
<p>The bill was supported by all parties.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town parliamentary office +2721 403-2502</p>
